diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 5ee3930c7..0b3267c26 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -290,7 +290,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 ### UI (Common)
 
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5513+) **Optionally** support **upscaling font size (i.e. font size)** regardless of game resolution. This affects **main interface** (city screen, map view, `city_billboard`/`CITYBILLBOARD`), **advisors**, **sevopedia**, most of **diplomacy screen** (when it was possible) in [CvDiplomacy.py](/Assets/Python/CvDiplomacy.py) and `CvPlayer::getItemTradeString` (for trading table), **Event Log** window (as of now only **Event Log** and **Combat Log** tabs are supported) and **event message popup** (top-center) in [CvUtil.py](/Assets/Python/CvUtil.py) and [CvEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/CvEventManager.py) and `CvDLLInterfaceIFaceBase::addMessage` (note: Event related message upscaling **only applies to new messages written after upscaling is enabled**, not to previously written event messages before upscaling was applied), miscallenous screens such as the [CvEraMovieScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvEraMovieScreen.py) (i.e. the e.g., "You have entered the Renaissance era!" screen), [CvWonderMovieScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvWonderMovieScreen.py), (from hardcoded `<font=4b>` to SAS FONT `TITLE` (more readable without bold)), [CvSpaceShipScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvSpaceShipScreen.py), and other places where font size could be changed. Made some **UI adjustments when needed to accomodate the larger text**. Upscaling text can be **useful for high resolution displays** (where text appears very small), but may **also improve readability at smaller resolutions** (like 1920*1080 or lower). A **simple way to upscale all text to max font size** is for example to set `SAS_UI_FONT_TINY`, `SAS_UI_FONT_BODY`, `SAS_UI_FONT_LABEL`, `SAS_UI_FONT_TITLE` and `SAS_UI_FONT_HOVER` all to max font size which is 4. See [GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml) and related places for the change.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5530+) **Upscaling adjustments** include generally to expand them so text does not overflow, or notably: smaller sevopedia leaders item row (else AI Personality Panel's upscaled text overfills), **smaller Sevopedia speeds first column** (only at **lower resolutions** since these don't have enough horizontal room per column to show them without clipping),  **overwrite city `billboard` xml** in [CIV4DetailManager.xml](/Assets/XML/Misc/CIV4DetailManager.xml) **at runtime** via [SASBillboardScale.py](/Assets/Python/SASBillboardScale.py) (**tunable per font size**), increase **GP bar size** and reduce **tech bar size** in **main interface (common)**, **do not upscale icons** in the Foreign Diplomacy Advisor's **Glance Tab** when text is upscaled and there are **>= 2 icons** (e.g., worst enemy + at war icons) (See [KI#116](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#116---worked-around-foreign-diplomacy-advisor-glance-tab-clips-trailing-status-icons-at-upscaled-label-fonts)), added **attitude icon chars** in [GameFont.tga](/Assets/res/Fonts/GameFont.tga) (21x20 icon size): previously they existed only in [GameFont_75.tga](/Assets/res/Fonts/GameFont_75.tga) (16x16 icon size), causing attitude icon chars to **disappear** (e.g., in Score Tab) **when font was upscaled (attitude font size >= 3)** (see [KI#117](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#117---fixed-score-tab-attitude-icon-chars-disappearing-at-upscaled-label-fonts-sas_ui_font_label-34)), increase **vertical spacing** in Info screen's **Graph Tab** between **leader lines** when text is upscaled (label > 3), **dynamically adjust** the Info Screen's **Graph tab**'s legend (i.e. leaders') **line height** (**reduced** when there are **many leaders** (e.g., > 36) but **expanded if vertical resolution is high** enough to accomodate it (e.g., >= 1440p)), and adjust legend **line width** depending on **font size** (label >= 3) (and further enlarge it for long leader names e.g., "Willhem van Oranje").
